{"full":"hf:lfoppiano/document-qa","spaceId":"lfoppiano/document-qa","name":"Scientific Document Insights Q/A","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["streamlit","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":16,"created":"2023-10-23T01:16:03.000Z","updated":"2026-03-27T16:04:06.000Z","license":"apache-2.0","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://lfoppiano-document-qa.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/lfoppiano/document-qa","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T17:53:24.334Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T17:53:24.334Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T17:53:24.334Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"📝","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["NOTE: The LLM API is kindly provided by Modal.com which offers 30$/month for computing. When these are done, the app will stop answering. 😅","Question/Answering on scientific documents using LLMs. The tool can be customized to use different types of LLM APIs. The streamlit application demonstrates the implementation of a RAG (Retrieval Augmented Generation) on scientific documents. Different from most of the projects, we focus on scientific articles and extract text from a structured document. We target only the full text using Grobid which provides cleaner results than the raw PDF2Text converter (which is comparable with most of the other solutions).","Additionally, this frontend provides the visualisation of named entities on LLM responses to extract physical quantities, measurements (with grobid-quantities) and materials mentions (with grobid-superconductors)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/lfoppiano/document-qa/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"856c5f60fe23fb469f93e3a322d1fb58a897747ee120a4ce5aa69f007eab6e13","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T17:53:24.402Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T17:53:24.402Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"